 "error_model": "Unlike eventlog.design_study.measured_extraction_study (independent per-date errors drawn from the type-matched date errors of the v2 adapter), this draws the error of each core interval from the within-note interval errors measured on the 700 held-out notes (diagnose.py / resolve_relative.py): for a pair of DAY-precision gold events in one note, err = predicted span - true span, so errors that share an anchor inside a note stay correlated.  An interval is lost with the measured share of pairs whose two endpoints were not both found (right type, DAY precision).  Negative spans are excluded as in the detector.  Extra predicted events are not modelled.",
